==German==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|schicken||lang=gmh}} "to outfit oneself, fit in, arrange appropriately", causative of {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|geschehen|geschehen, geschēn|lang=gmh}} "to happen, rush" from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|giskehan|lang=goh}} "to happen" from {{proto|Germanic|skihanan|to run, move quickly|lang=de}} from {{proto|Indo-European|skek-|to run, jump, spring|lang=de}}. Akin to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|sceon|scēon|lang=ang}} "to happen", {{etyl|nl|-}} {{l|nl|schielijk|''schie''lijk}} "hasty". More at {{l|en|chic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃɪkŋ̩/|/ˈʃɪkən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-schicken.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}} {{attention|de}}

# {{transitive|lang=de}} to [[send]]
# {{reflexive|lang=de}} to [[hurry]] (rare)
# {{reflexive|lang=de}} to be decent, to be appropriate

